<%- include('../../partials/policy-start') %>
<p class="lead">Everyone who handles food should be able to get certified. We build this course to work for people using a keyboard, a screen reader, magnification or other assistive technology.</p>

<h2>What we do</h2>
<ul>
  <li>We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 at level AA.</li>
  <li>Every chapter has a full written lesson, so the material isn’t only available on video.</li>
  <li>The site works with a keyboard alone, and uses headings, labels and landmarks that screen readers can follow.</li>
  <li>Text and controls meet contrast guidelines, and pages stay usable when zoomed to 200%.</li>
  <li>If your device asks for reduced motion, the site turns off its animations.</li>
  <li>Lessons and quizzes work on phones and tablets as well as computers.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The final exam</h2>
<p>The exam needs a camera, a microphone and a computer, because identity checks and proctoring are what make the certificate trustworthy. If a disability or medical condition makes any part of the exam difficult, email us before you start. We’ll discuss what we can arrange for you.</p>

<h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2>
<p>If something on the site doesn’t work for you, email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>. Tell us the page and what happened. We reply within two business days and can provide course material in another format on request.</p>
<%- include('../../partials/policy-end') %>
